  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Given an array AAA of NNN integers. Consider an arbitrary **non negative** integer XXX(initially, **score is zero**).\n\nWe will **sequentially** perform the following operation for indices 1,2,3,....N:1,2,3,....N:1,2,3,....N:\n\nFor ithi^{th}ith operation,\n\n\nIf X=AiX = A_iX=Ai​ then add XXX to scorescorescore.\nOtherwise, assign X:=X⊕AiX := X \\oplus A_iX:=X⊕Ai​.\nWhere ⊕\\oplus⊕ is bitwise **XOR** operation.\n\n**Note:** when XXX matches AiA_iAi​ during ithi^{th}ith operation, you are not updating XXX.\n\nYou are tasked to print the **maximum** achievable scorescorescore after doing NNN operations by choosing optimal **initial value** of integer XXX.\n\n\nInput Format\nThe first line contains single integer TTT −-− the number of testcases. For each testcase,\n\n\n\nthe first line contains a single integer NNN −-− the size of the array AAA.\nthe second line contains NNN space-separated integers, A1,A2,⋯ ,ANA_1, A_2, \\cdots, A_NA1​,A2​,⋯,AN​ −-− the elements of array AAA.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each testcase, print a single line containing a single integer −-− maximum possible scorescorescore.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤2⋅1051 \\leq T\\leq 2\\cdot 10^51≤T≤2⋅105",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\leq N\\leq 2\\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Ai≤1091 \\leq A_i\\leq 10^91≤Ai​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all testcases doesn't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n2\n1 2\n3\n1 1 1\n4\n2 1 3 3",
        "output": "2\n3\n8",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTestcase 1:\n\n\nIf initial State: X=0X = 0X=0 and score =0=0=0,\n\nAt i=1i = 1i=1:  Since X≠1X \\neq 1X=1, update X→X⊕A1=0⊕1=1X \\to X \\oplus A_1 = 0 \\oplus 1 = 1X→X⊕A1​=0⊕1=1 and score is still zero.\nAt i=2i = 2i=2:  Again X≠2X \\neq 2X=2, update X→X⊕A2=1⊕2=3X \\to X \\oplus A_2 = 1 \\oplus 2 = 3X→X⊕A2​=1⊕2=3 and score is still zero.\nFinal Score: 000\n\n\n\nIf initial State: X=3X = 3X=3 and score =0=0=0,\n\nAt i=1i = 1i=1:  Since X≠1X \\neq 1X=1, update X→X⊕A1=3⊕1=2X \\to X \\oplus A_1 = 3 \\oplus 1 = 2X→X⊕A1​=3⊕1=2 and score is still zero.\nAt i=2i = 2i=2:  Now, X=2X = 2X=2, so add XXX to the score and XXX is not updated.\nFinal Score: 222 (Maximum possible score).\n\n\n\nTestcase 2:\n\nIf initial State: X=1X = 1X=1 and score =0=0=0,\n\nAt i=1,2,3i = 1, 2, 3i=1,2,3:   Since X=1X = 1X=1 and X=AiX = A_iX=Ai​ throughout, no update in XXX is performed, and 111 is added to score every time.\nFinal Score: 333 (Maximum possible score)."
      }
    ]
  },
